    "algorithm": "Build inverse differences phi(x_0,...,x_{k-1},x_j) by the recursive table. Set tail=b_(N-1); for k=N-2 down through 1 set tail=b_k+(query-x_k)/tail; return y_0+(query-x_0)/tail.",
    "query_at_node": "Return that node's y_i exactly after validating that all required inverse differences are defined.",
    "degenerate_rule": "Port validity uses ordered IEEE-754 binary64 operations. A rounded binary64 inverse-difference denominator, diagonal coefficient, or continued-fraction tail is accepted only when its magnitude is strictly greater than 1/32+2^-32 and strictly less than 64-2^-32; every other table intermediate and output must be finite and strictly below 64-2^-32 in magnitude. Near-poles inside the lower guard band are invalid. The independent exact-rational system checks rank, exact sample/query denominators, and values as a separate cross-check for the pinned workload cases, not as an extra global port precondition.",
